IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nad-dates`

-- Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT) -- the rules a person bringing a discrimination, sexual harassment or victimisation
-- complaint meets: the attributes and the meaning of discrimination (Part 3 Division 1, ss 19-21), the other prohibited
-- conduct (Part 3 Division 2, ss 22-24, 26, 27), the areas of activity (Part 4, ss 28-49A, as an input), the exemptions a
-- respondent may rely on (Part 4's exemptions, ss 30, 35-37, 39, 40, 42-45, 47, 49, and Part 5, ss 50-59), the complaint
-- machinery as it meets the complainant (Part 6: ss 60, 65, 66, 66D, 66F, 71, 72, 79-81, 86-88, 91, 105), the appeal
-- time limit (s 106), and the transitional provisions on which version applies (ss 116, 122, 123, 126-128).
--
-- This module holds the law. The questions are asked in nad-seat.l4, which IMPORTs it and never restates a rule.
-- Nothing here is exported.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no rule answers JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no ("means", "takes place if",
-- "does not apply", "shall not", "cannot", an "if", "where" or "unless" condition that fails, "only"); or NOTHING where
-- the Act does not answer on the facts given, with a "NOTHING-kind" comment. In particular, an exemption that is limited
-- by its own wording (the ground, the dealing or the kind of body it names) answers NOTHING outside those words, and
-- JUST FALSE when its own "if" or "where" condition fails. Judgments the Act hands to someone else ("reasonable",
-- "satisfied", "genuine", "in good faith", "reasonably necessary") are inputs: the answer is conditional on them.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Not an official version of the Anti-Discrimination Act 1992 (NT). Copyright in Northern Territory
-- legislation is owned by the Northern Territory. Quoted under the Northern Territory copyright policy of 8 October 1996;
-- see SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Anti-Discrimination Act 1992`

§§ `Days fixed by the Act and its endnotes`

-- s 2 and the endnotes: the Act commenced on 1 August 1993 (Gaz G30, 28 July 1993). s 116(1): "This Act does not apply
-- to prohibited conduct which took place before the commencement of this Act." Also the commencement in s 49(2).
`the commencement day` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 8 1993

-- s 121: "commencement means the commencement of section 3 of the amending Act" (Anti-Discrimination Amendment Act 2022);
-- the endnotes: all but ss 8, 9, 26-31, 33-35, 40, 42 and 44 commenced on 3 July 2023 (Gaz G11, 25 May 2023).
`the 2022 amendments day` MEANS `the calendar date` 3 7 2023

-- s 126(3), s 127: the commencement of ss 4 and 5 of the Anti-Discrimination Amendment Act 2025; the endnotes: "rem:
-- 31 October 2025 (s 2(1))".
`the 2025 amendments day` MEANS `the calendar date` 31 10 2025

-- s 128(3): the commencement of Part 3 of the Anti-Discrimination Amendment Act 2025; the endnotes: "pt 3: 27 July 2026".
`the 2025 Part 3 day` MEANS `the calendar date` 27 7 2026

-- A small helper for the many "if" conditions: JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE.
GIVEN b IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`yes or no` b MEANS
    IF b
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- An exemption limited by its own wording (the ground, the dealing, the body) and then by an "if" condition: NOTHING
-- outside its wording (NOTHING-kind: limited by its own wording), then JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE on the condition.
GIVEN `within its wording` IS A BOOLEAN, `its condition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`within` `within its wording` `then if` `its condition` MEANS
    IF NOT `within its wording`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE `yes or no` `its condition`

§§ `s 19 -- the attributes`

-- s 19(1): "a person shall not discriminate against another person on the ground of any of the following attributes".
-- s 4: "attribute means an attribute referred to in section 19". The s 4 definitions of the attributes (race,
-- disability, relationship status, irrelevant criminal record and the rest) are glossed in the seat's descriptions;
-- whether a person has one is asked.
DECLARE `Attribute` IS ONE OF
    `race (including colour, descent, nationality, ethnic or national origin, being an immigrant)`
    `language, including signed language`
    `sex`
    `gender identity`
    `sexual orientation`
    `sex characteristics`
    `age`
    `relationship status`
    `accommodation status`
    `employment status`
    `employment in sex work or engaging in sex work, now or in the past`
    `pregnancy`
    `carer responsibilities`
    `breastfeeding`
    `disability`
    `HIV/hepatitis status`
    `being subjected to domestic violence`
    `trade union or employer association activity`
    `religious belief or activity`
    `political opinion, affiliation or activity`
    `an irrelevant medical record`
    `an irrelevant criminal record`
    `having my details published under s 66M of the Fines and Penalties (Recovery) Act 2001`
    `association with a person who has, or is believed to have, one of these attributes`
    `something else not listed`

-- "attribute means": a closed definition, so JUST FALSE for anything else.
GIVEN a IS AN `Attribute`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19 -- it is an attribute` a MEANS
    `yes or no` (NOT (a EQUALS `something else not listed`))

§§ `s 28 and Part 4 -- the areas of activity`

DECLARE `Area` IS ONE OF
    `education (s 29)`
    `work (s 31)`
    `a professional, trade, industry or employer organisation (s 32)`
    `a body that grants a qualification or authorisation for a profession, trade or business (s 33)`
    `an employment agency (s 34)`
    `accommodation (s 38)`
    `goods, services and facilities (s 41)`
    `a club (s 46)`
    `insurance or superannuation (s 48)`
    `the administration of a Territory law or government program (s 49A)`
    `none of these areas`

-- s 4: "club means an incorporated or unincorporated association of not less than 30 members". The other conditions of
-- the definition (purpose, funds) are folded into the person's choice of the area.
GIVEN `the number of members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4 -- it is a club` `the number of members` IF `the number of members` AT LEAST 30

§§ `ss 20, 21 -- discrimination`

-- s 20(1): "discrimination includes: (a) any distinction, restriction, exclusion or preference made on the basis of an
-- attribute that has the effect of nullifying or impairing equality of opportunity; and (b) harassment on the basis of an
-- attribute, in an area of activity referred to in Part 4." (2): "discrimination takes place if a person treats or
-- proposes to treat another person who has or had, or is believed to have or had: (a) an attribute; or (b) a
-- characteristic imputed to appertain to an attribute; or (c) a characteristic imputed to appertain generally to persons
-- with an attribute, less favourably than a person who has not, or is believed not to have, such an attribute." (3): the
-- attribute need not be "the sole or dominant ground", and the discriminator need not regard the treatment as less
-- favourable. (4): "The motive ... is ... irrelevant." s 21(1): less favourable treatment "because the person has an
-- assistance animal" is discrimination on the ground of disability, whatever the practice towards other animals (21(2)).
-- s 28: "This Act applies to prohibited conduct in the areas of" the seven areas. Parts 4's sections list the dealings
-- in each area, each ending with less favourable treatment "in any way in connection with" it (except s 48(1), s 49A).
--
-- Answers: JUST FALSE for a ground that is not an attribute ("means"); NOTHING outside the areas (s 28 and s 20(1) state
-- the scope without "only": NOTHING-kind: limited by its own wording; fork F2), and for a body of fewer than 30 members
-- chosen as a club (NOTHING-kind: points elsewhere, finding 4); JUST TRUE where s 20(2) or s 21 is met, or a head of
-- s 20(1) holds ("includes"); NOTHING otherwise (NOTHING-kind: "includes" leaves the list open).
GIVEN a IS AN `Attribute`
      area IS AN `Area`
      `club members` IS A NUMBER
      `treated less favourably because of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a distinction impairing equality of opportunity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `harassed because of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `treated less favourably because of an assistance animal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 19-21 -- I was discriminated against` a area `club members` `treated less favourably because of it` `a distinction impairing equality of opportunity` `harassed because of it` `treated less favourably because of an assistance animal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF a EQUALS `something else not listed` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF area EQUALS `none of these areas` THEN NOTHING
        IF (area EQUALS `a club (s 46)`) AND (NOT (`s 4 -- it is a club` `club members`)) THEN NOTHING
        IF `treated less favourably because of it` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `a distinction impairing equality of opportunity` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `harassed because of it` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (a EQUALS `disability`) AND `treated less favourably because of an assistance animal` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 20A, s 20B -- inciting hatred, serious contempt or severe ridicule`

DECLARE `Purpose under s 20B` IS ONE OF
    `performing, exhibiting or distributing an artistic work`
    `a statement, publication, discussion or debate for a genuine academic, artistic, scientific or public interest purpose`
    `a fair and accurate report of an event or matter of public interest`
    `a fair comment on an event or matter of public interest that expresses a genuine belief of the person commenting`
    `none of these purposes`

-- s 20A(1): "A person must not do an act that: (a) is reasonably likely, in all the circumstances, to incite hatred
-- towards, serious contempt for or severe ridicule of, another person or a group of people; and (b) is done because of an
-- attribute". (2): "Subsection (1) does not apply to an act done in private." (3): "an act is taken not to be done in
-- private if it: (a) causes words, sounds, images or writing to be communicated to the public; or (b) is done in a
-- public place; or (c) is done in the sight or hearing of people who are in a public place." s 20B: "Section 20A does not
-- prevent anything said or done reasonably and in good faith" for the listed purposes.
-- Answers: NOTHING where (a) or (b) fails (the prohibition's own wording; NOTHING-kind: limited by its own wording);
-- JUST FALSE where the act is private ("does not apply") or s 20B covers it ("does not prevent"); JUST TRUE otherwise.
GIVEN `reasonably likely to incite` IS A BOOLEAN
      `because of an attribute` IS A BOOLEAN
      `communicated to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `done in a public place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the sight or hearing of people in a public place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `otherwise done in private` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reasonably and in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose` IS A `Purpose under s 20B`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20A -- the act was prohibited` `reasonably likely to incite` `because of an attribute` `communicated to the public` `done in a public place` `in the sight or hearing of people in a public place` `otherwise done in private` `reasonably and in good faith` `the purpose` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`reasonably likely to incite` AND `because of an attribute`) THEN NOTHING
        IF `the act is private` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `s 20B covers it` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the act is private` MEANS
            `otherwise done in private` AND (NOT (`communicated to the public` OR `done in a public place` OR `in the sight or hearing of people in a public place`))
        `s 20B covers it` MEANS
            `reasonably and in good faith` AND (NOT (`the purpose` EQUALS `none of these purposes`))

§§ `s 22 -- sexual harassment`

DECLARE `Sexual conduct` IS ONE OF
    `an act of physical intimacy`
    `a demand or request for sexual favours, direct or implied`
    `a remark with sexual connotations`
    `other conduct of a sexual nature`
    `none of these`

-- s 22(2): "Sexual harassment takes place if a person: (a) subjects another person to an unwelcome act of physical
-- intimacy; or (b) makes an unwelcome demand or request ... for sexual favours ...; or (c) makes an unwelcome remark with
-- sexual connotations; or (d) engages in any other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature, and: (e) that person does so:
-- (i) with the intention of offending, humiliating or intimidating the other person; or (ii) in circumstances where a
-- reasonable person would have anticipated the possibility that the other person would be offended, humiliated or
-- intimidated by the conduct; or (f) that other person is, or reasonably believes they are likely to be, subjected to
-- some detriment if they object". "Takes place if": JUST FALSE where the conditions fail. s 22(3)'s circumstances are
-- for the (e)(ii) judgment, which is an input. s 22 names no area (fork F3).
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A `Sexual conduct`
      `it was unwelcome` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they intended to offend, humiliate or intimidate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a reasonable person would have anticipated offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `detriment if I objected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22 -- I was sexually harassed` `the conduct` `it was unwelcome` `they intended to offend, humiliate or intimidate` `a reasonable person would have anticipated offence` `detriment if I objected` MEANS
    `yes or no`
        (    (NOT (`the conduct` EQUALS `none of these`))
         AND `it was unwelcome`
         AND (   `they intended to offend, humiliate or intimidate`
              OR `a reasonable person would have anticipated offence`
              OR `detriment if I objected`))

§§ `s 23 -- victimisation`

DECLARE `Reason for the detriment` IS ONE OF
    `I made, or intend to make, a complaint`
    `I gave, or intend to give, evidence or information in connection with proceedings under the Act`
    `I alleged, or intend to allege, that a person did something that would contravene the Act`
    `I did something else in relation to a person under or by reference to the Act`
    `another reason`

-- s 23(1): "A person shall not victimise another person because the other person" did one of the four things. (2):
-- "Victimisation takes place if a person subjects or threatens to subject another person or an associate of the other
-- person to any detriment." (3): "Subsection (1)(c) does not apply to ... an allegation that is false and not made in
-- good faith." Answers: JUST FALSE without a detriment ("takes place if") or for a false allegation not in good faith
-- ("does not apply"); NOTHING for another reason (the prohibition's own wording; NOTHING-kind: limited by its own
-- wording); JUST TRUE otherwise.
GIVEN `a detriment, done or threatened, to me or my associate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reason` IS A `Reason for the detriment`
      `the allegation was false and not made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23 -- I was victimised` `a detriment, done or threatened, to me or my associate` `the reason` `the allegation was false and not made in good faith` MEANS
    IF NOT `a detriment, done or threatened, to me or my associate`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the reason`
         WHEN `another reason` THEN NOTHING
         WHEN `I alleged, or intend to allege, that a person did something that would contravene the Act` THEN
             `yes or no` (NOT `the allegation was false and not made in good faith`)
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 24 -- the duty to accommodate a special need`

-- s 24(1): "A person must reasonably accommodate a special need that another person has because of an attribute." (2)(b):
-- "reasonable accommodation of a special need takes place when a person acts in a way that reasonably provides for the
-- special need". (3): whether they reasonably provided depends on all the circumstances (the need, the cost and the
-- number who benefit, their finances, disruption, benefit or detriment to all): a judgment, asked as an input.
-- Answers (did they contravene the duty?): NOTHING without a special need because of an attribute (the duty's own
-- wording; NOTHING-kind: limited by its own wording); JUST FALSE where they reasonably provided ("takes place when");
-- JUST TRUE otherwise. s 58 (accommodation unreasonable) is a general exemption, asked separately.
GIVEN `a special need because of an attribute` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they reasonably provided for it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24 -- they failed to accommodate my special need` `a special need because of an attribute` `they reasonably provided for it` MEANS
    `within` `a special need because of an attribute` `then if` (NOT `they reasonably provided for it`)

§§ `s 39 -- alterations to accommodation`

-- s 39: "A person must not discriminate against a person with a disability by failing or refusing to allow the person to
-- alter accommodation to meet the person's special needs if: (a) the alteration is at the expense of that person; and
-- (b) the alteration does not require an alteration to the accommodation of another person; and (c) the restoration of
-- the accommodation to its previous condition is reasonably practicable; and (d) the person undertakes at the person's
-- own expense to restore the accommodation ... before leaving it, and it is reasonably likely that the person will do
-- so." Answers (must they allow it?): NOTHING without a disability (NOTHING-kind: limited by its own wording); JUST TRUE
-- where (a)-(d) all hold; JUST FALSE where one fails ("if").
GIVEN `I have a disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at my expense` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no other person's accommodation altered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `restoration reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I undertake to restore it and am reasonably likely to` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39 -- they must allow the alteration` `I have a disability` `at my expense` `no other person's accommodation altered` `restoration reasonably practicable` `I undertake to restore it and am reasonably likely to` MEANS
    `within` `I have a disability` `then if`
        (    `at my expense`
         AND `no other person's accommodation altered`
         AND `restoration reasonably practicable`
         AND `I undertake to restore it and am reasonably likely to`)

§§ `s 26 -- unnecessary information`

-- s 26(1): "A person shall not ask another person ... to supply information on which unlawful discrimination might be
-- based." (2): it "does not apply to a request that is necessary to comply with, or is specifically authorised by" a law
-- of the Territory or the Commonwealth, a court or tribunal order, an award, an industrial agreement or an order of the
-- Commissioner. (3): it "does not apply if the person proves ... that the information was reasonably required for a
-- purpose that did not involve discrimination." Answers: NOTHING where unlawful discrimination could not be based on it
-- (NOTHING-kind: limited by its own wording); JUST FALSE under (2) or (3); JUST TRUE otherwise.
GIVEN `discrimination might be based on it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `required or authorised by a law, order, award, agreement or the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they prove it was reasonably required for a non-discriminatory purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26 -- asking me was prohibited` `discrimination might be based on it` `required or authorised by a law, order, award, agreement or the Commissioner` `they prove it was reasonably required for a non-discriminatory purpose` MEANS
    `within` `discrimination might be based on it` `then if`
        (NOT (`required or authorised by a law, order, award, agreement or the Commissioner` OR `they prove it was reasonably required for a non-discriminatory purpose`))

§§ `s 27, s 105 -- who else is liable`

-- s 27(2): "A person who causes, instructs, induces, incites, assists or promotes another person to contravene this Act
-- is jointly and severally liable with the other person for the contravention". Answers: JUST TRUE where both hold;
-- NOTHING otherwise (NOTHING-kind: limited by its own wording).
GIVEN `they caused, instructed, induced, incited, assisted or promoted it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person contravened the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27 -- they are jointly liable` `they caused, instructed, induced, incited, assisted or promoted it` `the other person contravened the Act` MEANS
    `within` (`they caused, instructed, induced, incited, assisted or promoted it` AND `the other person contravened the Act`) `then if` TRUE

-- s 105(1): "If: (a) a worker of a person does an act in connection with the person's work that is unlawful under this
-- Act; or (b) an agent of a person does an act in connection with the person's duties as an agent that is unlawful ...,
-- this Act applies in relation to the person as if the person had also done the act." (2): "Subsection (1) does not
-- apply if the person shows that the person took all reasonable steps to prevent" it. (3) lists the matters for that
-- judgment, which is an input. Answers: JUST FALSE where (1) fails ("if") or (2) is shown ("does not apply").
GIVEN `done by their worker or agent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in connection with their work or the agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act was unlawful under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they show they took all reasonable steps to prevent it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105 -- they are liable as if they had done it` `done by their worker or agent` `in connection with their work or the agency` `the act was unlawful under the Act` `they show they took all reasonable steps to prevent it` MEANS
    `yes or no`
        (    `done by their worker or agent`
         AND `in connection with their work or the agency`
         AND `the act was unlawful under the Act`
         AND (NOT `they show they took all reasonable steps to prevent it`))

§§ `ss 35-37, 127 -- exemptions in the area of work`

DECLARE `Work exemption` IS ONE OF
    `s 35(1)(a) -- reasonable terms for a restricted capacity`
    `s 35(1)(b)(i) -- a genuine occupational qualification`
    `s 35(1)(b)(ii) -- unable to perform the inherent requirements`
    `s 35(2) -- work in their home`
    `s 35A -- employment status`
    `s 35B -- a religious educational institution`
    `s 36 -- a standard starting or retirement age`
    `s 37 -- an irrelevant criminal record and vulnerable people`

-- s 35(1): "A person may discriminate ... in the area of work: (a) by fixing reasonable terms and conditions if that
-- other person, because of age or disability, has a restricted capacity to do the work; or (b) if the discrimination is
-- based: (i) on a genuine occupational qualification which the other person is required to fill; or (ii) on the other
-- person's inability to adequately perform the inherent requirements of the work even where the special need of the other
-- person has been or were to be accommodated." (2): "may discriminate in offering work where the work is to be performed
-- in the person's home." s 35A: "on the ground of employment status in relation to something mentioned in section
-- 31(1)(a) to (c) if the discrimination is reasonable, justifiable and proportionate". s 35B(1): an educational authority
-- operating an institution "in accordance with the doctrine of a particular religion may discriminate ... in the area of
-- work ... if the discrimination: (a) is on the ground of religious belief or activity; and (b) is in good faith to avoid
-- offending the religious sensitivities of a reasonable person of the particular religion." (3): it does "not apply ...
-- unless the educational authority" produces the written policy and makes it available to employees and prospective
-- employees. s 127: "Section 35B does not apply in respect of any person who works for an educational institution at the
-- time section 5 of the amending Act commences" (31 October 2025). s 36: "may discriminate on the grounds of age by
-- imposing a standard age for commencement of work or a standard retirement age." s 37(1): "on the grounds of irrelevant
-- criminal record in the area of work if: (a) the work principally involves the care, instruction or supervision of
-- vulnerable persons; and (b) the discrimination is reasonably necessary to protect" them.
-- Answers: NOTHING outside each exemption's own wording (the ground, the dealing, fixing reasonable terms, the kind of
-- institution, a standard age); JUST FALSE where its "if", "where" or "unless" fails or s 127 excludes it.
GIVEN e IS A `Work exemption`
      a IS AN `Attribute`
      `in offering work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a restricted capacity because of age or disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the terms fixed are reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a genuine occupational qualification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `unable to perform the inherent requirements even if accommodated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work is in their home` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reasonable, justifiable and proportionate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a religious educational institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in good faith to avoid offending religious sensitivities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the written policy was produced and made available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I worked there on 31 October 2025` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a standard starting or retirement age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `work principally caring for, instructing or supervising vulnerable persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reasonably necessary to protect them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 35-37 -- the work exemption applies` e a `in offering work` `a restricted capacity because of age or disability` `the terms fixed are reasonable` `a genuine occupational qualification` `unable to perform the inherent requirements even if accommodated` `the work is in their home` `reasonable, justifiable and proportionate` `a religious educational institution` `in good faith to avoid offending religious sensitivities` `the written policy was produced and made available` `I worked there on 31 October 2025` `a standard starting or retirement age` `work principally caring for, instructing or supervising vulnerable persons` `reasonably necessary to protect them` MEANS
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `s 35(1)(a) -- reasonable terms for a restricted capacity` THEN
        `within` `the terms fixed are reasonable` `then if` `a restricted capacity because of age or disability`
    WHEN `s 35(1)(b)(i) -- a genuine occupational qualification` THEN
        `yes or no` `a genuine occupational qualification`
    WHEN `s 35(1)(b)(ii) -- unable to perform the inherent requirements` THEN
        `yes or no` `unable to perform the inherent requirements even if accommodated`
    WHEN `s 35(2) -- work in their home` THEN
        `within` `in offering work` `then if` `the work is in their home`
    WHEN `s 35A -- employment status` THEN
        `within` ((a EQUALS `employment status`) AND `in offering work`) `then if` `reasonable, justifiable and proportionate`
    WHEN `s 35B -- a religious educational institution` THEN
        IF NOT `a religious educational institution`
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE `yes or no`
                 (    (NOT `I worked there on 31 October 2025`)
                  AND (a EQUALS `religious belief or activity`)
                  AND `in good faith to avoid offending religious sensitivities`
                  AND `the written policy was produced and made available`)
    WHEN `s 36 -- a standard starting or retirement age` THEN
        `within` ((a EQUALS `age`) AND `a standard starting or retirement age`) `then if` TRUE
    WHEN `s 37 -- an irrelevant criminal record and vulnerable people` THEN
        `within` (a EQUALS `an irrelevant criminal record`) `then if` (`work principally caring for, instructing or supervising vulnerable persons` AND `reasonably necessary to protect them`)

§§ `ss 30, 40 -- exemptions in education and accommodation`

DECLARE `Education or accommodation exemption` IS ONE OF
    `s 30(1) -- a single-sex educational institution`
    `s 30(3) -- an educational institution for students with a disability`
    `s 40(1) -- their own or a near relative's home`
    `s 40(2) -- accommodation at a single-sex educational institution`
    `s 40(2B) -- accommodation at an educational institution for students with a disability`
    `s 40(3) -- accommodation of a religious body`
    `s 40(4) -- accommodation of a charitable body`

-- s 30(1): an authority operating an institution "wholly or mainly for students of a particular sex may exclude
-- applicants who are not of that sex." (3): the same for "students who have a general or specific disability". s 40(1):
-- "in deciding who is to reside in accommodation that forms part of, and is intended to continue to form part of, the
-- main home of the person or a near relative". (2), (2B): such an authority "may provide accommodation wholly or mainly
-- for students of that sex" (or "with that disability"). (3): accommodation "(i) under the direction or control of a body
-- established for religious purposes; and (ii) wholly within or directly attached to religious premises" if the
-- discrimination "(i) is in accordance with the doctrine of the religion concerned; and (ii) is necessary to avoid
-- offending the religious sensitivities"; (5): (3) "does not apply ... at any time at which a program that is funded by,
-- or conducted on behalf of, the Territory or the Commonwealth is being conducted at that accommodation." (4): "under the
-- direction or control of a body established for a charitable purpose" if "in accordance with the particular purpose for
-- which the accommodation was established". Answers: ss 30, 40(1), (2), (2B) are permissions limited by their own
-- wording (NOTHING outside it, JUST TRUE within); (3), (4) JUST FALSE where their "if" fails, (3) also under (5).
GIVEN e IS AN `Education or accommodation exemption`
      `an institution wholly or mainly for students of one sex` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am not of that sex` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an institution wholly or mainly for students with a particular disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I do not have that disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was about my admission as a student` IS A BOOLEAN
      `accommodation provided wholly or mainly for those students` IS A BOOLEAN
      `deciding who lives in their or a near relative's main home` IS A BOOLEAN
      `controlled by a religious body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `within or attached to a place of worship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in accordance with the doctrine` IS A BOOLEAN
      `necessary to avoid offending religious sensitivities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a Territory or Commonwealth program running there at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `controlled by a charitable body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in accordance with its charitable purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 30, 40 -- the exemption applies` e `an institution wholly or mainly for students of one sex` `I am not of that sex` `an institution wholly or mainly for students with a particular disability` `I do not have that disability` `it was about my admission as a student` `accommodation provided wholly or mainly for those students` `deciding who lives in their or a near relative's main home` `controlled by a religious body` `within or attached to a place of worship` `in accordance with the doctrine` `necessary to avoid offending religious sensitivities` `a Territory or Commonwealth program running there at the time` `controlled by a charitable body` `in accordance with its charitable purpose` MEANS
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `s 30(1) -- a single-sex educational institution` THEN
        `within` (`an institution wholly or mainly for students of one sex` AND `I am not of that sex` AND `it was about my admission as a student`) `then if` TRUE
    WHEN `s 30(3) -- an educational institution for students with a disability` THEN
        `within` (`an institution wholly or mainly for students with a particular disability` AND `I do not have that disability` AND `it was about my admission as a student`) `then if` TRUE
    WHEN `s 40(1) -- their own or a near relative's home` THEN
        `within` `deciding who lives in their or a near relative's main home` `then if` TRUE
    WHEN `s 40(2) -- accommodation at a single-sex educational institution` THEN
        `within` (`an institution wholly or mainly for students of one sex` AND `accommodation provided wholly or mainly for those students`) `then if` TRUE
    WHEN `s 40(2B) -- accommodation at an educational institution for students with a disability` THEN
        `within` (`an institution wholly or mainly for students with a particular disability` AND `accommodation provided wholly or mainly for those students`) `then if` TRUE
    WHEN `s 40(3) -- accommodation of a religious body` THEN
        `yes or no`
            (    `controlled by a religious body`
             AND `within or attached to a place of worship`
             AND `in accordance with the doctrine`
             AND `necessary to avoid offending religious sensitivities`
             AND (NOT `a Territory or Commonwealth program running there at the time`))
    WHEN `s 40(4) -- accommodation of a charitable body` THEN
        `yes or no` (`controlled by a charitable body` AND `in accordance with its charitable purpose`)

§§ `ss 42-45 -- exemptions for goods, services and facilities`

DECLARE `Goods and services exemption` IS ONE OF
    `s 42 -- a service only one sex can receive`
    `s 43 -- a place of cultural or religious significance`
    `s 44 -- an age-based benefit or concession`
    `s 45 -- a child to be accompanied by an adult`

-- s 4: "child means a person who has not attained the age of 18 years."
GIVEN `my age in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4 -- I am a child` `my age in years` IF `my age in years` LESS THAN 18

-- s 42: "Nothing in this Division applies to ... the provision of a service the nature of which is such that it can only
-- be provided to members of one sex." s 43(1): "may restrict access to land, a building or place of cultural or religious
-- significance by people who are not of a particular sex, age, race or religion if the restriction: (a) is in accordance
-- with the culture or the doctrine of the religion; and (b) is necessary to avoid offending the cultural or religious
-- sensitivities". s 44: "may supply benefits and concessions on the basis of age". s 45: "may require, as a term of
-- supplying goods, services or facilities to a child, that the child be accompanied by an adult if there is a reasonable
-- risk that a child could cause a disruption or endanger themselves, or others, if not accompanied". Answers: NOTHING
-- outside each provision's own wording; JUST FALSE where the "if" of s 43 or s 45 fails.
GIVEN e IS A `Goods and services exemption`
      a IS AN `Attribute`
      `a service only one sex can by its nature receive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `restricting access to a place of cultural or religious significance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in accordance with the culture or religious doctrine` IS A BOOLEAN
      `necessary to avoid offending cultural or religious sensitivities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a benefit or concession given on the basis of age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my age in years` IS A NUMBER
      `required to be accompanied by an adult` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a reasonable risk of disruption or danger if unaccompanied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 42-45 -- the exemption applies` e a `a service only one sex can by its nature receive` `restricting access to a place of cultural or religious significance` `in accordance with the culture or religious doctrine` `necessary to avoid offending cultural or religious sensitivities` `a benefit or concession given on the basis of age` `my age in years` `required to be accompanied by an adult` `a reasonable risk of disruption or danger if unaccompanied` MEANS
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `s 42 -- a service only one sex can receive` THEN
        `within` `a service only one sex can by its nature receive` `then if` TRUE
    WHEN `s 43 -- a place of cultural or religious significance` THEN
        `within` (`restricting access to a place of cultural or religious significance` AND `the ground is sex, age, race or religion`) `then if` (`in accordance with the culture or religious doctrine` AND `necessary to avoid offending cultural or religious sensitivities`)
    WHEN `s 44 -- an age-based benefit or concession` THEN
        `within` ((a EQUALS `age`) AND `a benefit or concession given on the basis of age`) `then if` TRUE
    WHEN `s 45 -- a child to be accompanied by an adult` THEN
        `within` ((`s 4 -- I am a child` `my age in years`) AND `required to be accompanied by an adult`) `then if` `a reasonable risk of disruption or danger if unaccompanied`
    WHERE
        `the ground is sex, age, race or religion` MEANS
               a EQUALS `sex`
            OR a EQUALS `age`
            OR a EQUALS `race (including colour, descent, nationality, ethnic or national origin, being an immigrant)`
            OR a EQUALS `religious belief or activity`

§§ `s 47 -- exemptions for clubs`

DECLARE `Club exemption` IS ONE OF
    `s 47(1) -- a club for a particular group`
    `s 47(2) -- a club for an age group`
    `s 47(3) -- sharing a club benefit between the sexes`

-- s 47(1): may discriminate "against applicants for membership of the club who are not members of the group of people
-- with an attribute for whom the club was established if the club operates wholly or mainly: (a) to preserve a minority
-- culture; or (b) to prevent or reduce disadvantage suffered by, or meet the special or particular needs of, people of
-- that group." (2): "on the ground of age in membership of the club if the club provides association wholly or mainly
-- for people of a specific age or age group." (3): "on the ground of sex: (b) if the discrimination occurs in relation to
-- the use or enjoyment of a benefit provided by the club where: (i) it is not practicable for the benefit to be used or
-- enjoyed simultaneously, or to the same extent, by different sexes; and (ii) either the same or an equivalent benefit is
-- provided for the use of different sexes separately ..., or different sexes are each entitled to a fair and reasonable
-- proportion of the use and enjoyment of the benefit." Answers: NOTHING outside each provision's own wording; JUST FALSE
-- where its "if" or "where" fails.
GIVEN e IS A `Club exemption`
      a IS AN `Attribute`
      `I applied for membership` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am not in the group the club was established for` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the club operates mainly to preserve a minority culture or for the group's disadvantage or needs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it concerns membership` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the club is mainly for a specific age group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it concerns the use of a club benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sexes cannot practicably share the benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an equivalent separate benefit or a fair share is provided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47 -- the club exemption applies` e a `I applied for membership` `I am not in the group the club was established for` `the club operates mainly to preserve a minority culture or for the group's disadvantage or needs` `it concerns membership` `the club is mainly for a specific age group` `it concerns the use of a club benefit` `the sexes cannot practicably share the benefit` `an equivalent separate benefit or a fair share is provided` MEANS
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `s 47(1) -- a club for a particular group` THEN
        `within` (`I applied for membership` AND `I am not in the group the club was established for`) `then if` `the club operates mainly to preserve a minority culture or for the group's disadvantage or needs`
    WHEN `s 47(2) -- a club for an age group` THEN
        `within` ((a EQUALS `age`) AND `it concerns membership`) `then if` `the club is mainly for a specific age group`
    WHEN `s 47(3) -- sharing a club benefit between the sexes` THEN
        `within` (a EQUALS `sex`) `then if` (`it concerns the use of a club benefit` AND `the sexes cannot practicably share the benefit` AND `an equivalent separate benefit or a fair share is provided`)

§§ `s 49 -- exemptions for insurance and superannuation`

DECLARE `Insurance exemption` IS ONE OF
    `s 49(1)(a) -- a standard under the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993`
    `s 49(1)(b) -- permitted by the Sex Discrimination Act 1984`
    `s 49(1)(c) -- complying with another Commonwealth Act`
    `s 49(1)(d)-(f) -- actuarial, statistical or other data, or other relevant factors`
    `s 49(2) -- an existing superannuation fund condition`

-- s 49(1): "may discriminate ... if one or more of the following is applicable: (a) the discrimination happens because
-- of the application of a standard in force under the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993 (Cth); (b) ... is
-- permitted under the Sex Discrimination Act 1984 ...; (c) ... happens in order to comply with or obtain the benefits of,
-- or to avoid penalties under, any other Act of the Commonwealth; (d) ... is based on reasonable actuarial or statistical
-- data from a source on which it is reasonable to rely and ... is reasonable having regard to that data and other
-- relevant factors; (e) if there is no reasonable actuarial or statistical data ..., ... is based on other data on which
-- it is reasonable to rely and ... is reasonable ...; (f) if there is no reasonable actuarial, statistical or other data
-- ..., ... is reasonable having regard to any other relevant factors." (2): "in the area of superannuation to the extent
-- that the discrimination is based on an existing superannuation fund condition and relates to a person who became a
-- member of the fund before the commencement of this Act or not more than 12 months after that commencement." (3): "a
-- superannuation fund condition in existence at the commencement". Answers: JUST FALSE where (1)'s "if" fails; for (2),
-- NOTHING outside superannuation (its own wording), JUST FALSE where the condition or the joining day fails (fork F1).
GIVEN e IS AN `Insurance exemption`
      `because of a standard under the SIS Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `permitted under the Sex Discrimination Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `to comply with, obtain benefits or avoid penalties under another Commonwealth Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reasonable actuarial or statistical data exists` IS A BOOLEAN
      `other reasonable data exists` IS A BOOLEAN
      `based on that data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reasonable having regard to the data and other relevant factors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is superannuation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `based on a fund condition existing on 1 August 1993` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I became a member` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49 -- the insurance exemption applies` e `because of a standard under the SIS Act` `permitted under the Sex Discrimination Act` `to comply with, obtain benefits or avoid penalties under another Commonwealth Act` `reasonable actuarial or statistical data exists` `other reasonable data exists` `based on that data` `reasonable having regard to the data and other relevant factors` `it is superannuation` `based on a fund condition existing on 1 August 1993` `the day I became a member` MEANS
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `s 49(1)(a) -- a standard under the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993` THEN
        `yes or no` `because of a standard under the SIS Act`
    WHEN `s 49(1)(b) -- permitted by the Sex Discrimination Act 1984` THEN
        `yes or no` `permitted under the Sex Discrimination Act`
    WHEN `s 49(1)(c) -- complying with another Commonwealth Act` THEN
        `yes or no` `to comply with, obtain benefits or avoid penalties under another Commonwealth Act`
    WHEN `s 49(1)(d)-(f) -- actuarial, statistical or other data, or other relevant factors` THEN
        `yes or no` (`head (d)` OR `head (e)` OR `head (f)`)
    WHEN `s 49(2) -- an existing superannuation fund condition` THEN
        `within` `it is superannuation` `then if`
            (    `based on a fund condition existing on 1 August 1993`
             AND (NOT (`the day I became a member` `is after` (`the anniversary` 1 `years after` `the commencement day`))))
    WHERE
        `head (d)` MEANS `reasonable actuarial or statistical data exists` AND `based on that data` AND `reasonable having regard to the data and other relevant factors`
        `head (e)` MEANS (NOT `reasonable actuarial or statistical data exists`) AND `other reasonable data exists` AND `based on that data` AND `reasonable having regard to the data and other relevant factors`
        `head (f)` MEANS (NOT `reasonable actuarial or statistical data exists`) AND (NOT `other reasonable data exists`) AND `reasonable having regard to the data and other relevant factors`

§§ `s 21(5) and Part 5 -- general exemptions`

DECLARE `General exemption` IS ONE OF
    `s 21(5) -- no evidence produced that the animal is an assistance animal`
    `s 50 -- a legal incapacity`
    `s 51 -- religious bodies`
    `s 52 -- a charitable provision in a will, deed or other instrument`
    `s 53 -- complying with a law, order, award, agreement or the Commissioner`
    `s 54 -- rights given for another person's pregnancy or childbirth`
    `s 55 -- public health`
    `s 56 -- competitive sport`
    `s 57 -- a special measure`
    `s 58 -- accommodating a special need would be unreasonable`
    `s 59 -- an exemption granted by the Commissioner`

DECLARE `Sport restriction` IS ONE OF
    `to people of one sex`
    `to people who can effectively compete`
    `to people of a specified age or age group`
    `to people with a general or specific disability`
    `on another basis`

-- s 21(5): nothing makes it unlawful to "(a) request a person with an assistance animal to produce evidence that the
-- animal is an assistance animal; and (b) if the person ... does not produce evidence ... discriminate against the person
-- on the ground that the person has the animal." s 50: "against another person who is subject to a legal incapacity if
-- that incapacity is relevant to the transaction". s 51: "This Act does not apply to or in relation to" ordination,
-- training of religious leaders, religious observance or practice, and acts of a religious body as part of them. s 52: a
-- discriminatory provision in a will, deed or other instrument that provides for charitable benefits, and acts to give
-- effect to it. s 53: "a person may do an act that is necessary to comply with, or is specifically authorised by" an
-- Act, regulation, order, award, an industrial agreement in existence at commencement, or the Commissioner's order,
-- guideline, code or advice. s 54: "by reason only of the fact that person A grants rights and privileges to a person
-- (person C) in connection with person C's pregnancy or childbirth." s 55: "on the ground of disability if the
-- discrimination is reasonably necessary to protect public health." s 56(1): "may restrict participation in a competitive
-- sporting activity: (a) to persons of a particular sex, if the restriction is reasonable having regard to the strength,
-- stamina or physique requirements of the activity; or (b) to people who can effectively compete; or (c) to people of a
-- specified age or age group; or (d) to people with a general or specific disability." (2): "(1)(a) does not apply to a
-- sporting activity for children who have not attained 12 years of age." (3): competitive sporting activity "does not
-- include" coaching, umpiring or refereeing, administration or a prescribed activity. s 57(1): "in a program, plan or
-- arrangement designed to promote equality of opportunity for a group of people who are disadvantaged or have a special
-- need because of an attribute." (2): "applies only until equality of opportunity has been achieved." s 58(1): "against
-- another person who has a special need ... if: (a) the other person would require special services or facilities; and
-- (b) it is unreasonable to require the person to supply" them. s 59: an exemption granted (for up to 3 years) or renewed
-- by the Commissioner.
-- Answers: NOTHING outside each provision's own wording; JUST FALSE where its "if" fails, where s 54's "only" is not met,
-- where s 56(2) or (3) excludes the case ("does not apply", "does not include"), or after equality is achieved (s 57(2)).
GIVEN e IS A `General exemption`
      a IS AN `Attribute`
      `because I have the animal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I did not produce evidence when asked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am subject to a legal incapacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is relevant to the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `religious ordination, training or observance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `giving effect to a charitable provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `necessary to comply with or authorised by a law, order, award, agreement or the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `only because they gave rights to another person for pregnancy or childbirth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reasonably necessary to protect public health` IS A BOOLEAN
      `restricting who takes part in a competitive sporting activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the restriction` IS A `Sport restriction`
      `reasonable for the strength, stamina or physique required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an activity for children under 12` IS A BOOLEAN
      `coaching, umpiring, refereeing or administration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a program for equality of opportunity for a disadvantaged group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `equality of opportunity has been achieved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I would require special services or facilities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `unreasonable to require them to supply them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a Commissioner's exemption in force covers it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Part 5 -- the general exemption applies` e a `because I have the animal` `I did not produce evidence when asked` `I am subject to a legal incapacity` `it is relevant to the transaction` `religious ordination, training or observance` `giving effect to a charitable provision` `necessary to comply with or authorised by a law, order, award, agreement or the Commissioner` `only because they gave rights to another person for pregnancy or childbirth` `reasonably necessary to protect public health` `restricting who takes part in a competitive sporting activity` `the restriction` `reasonable for the strength, stamina or physique required` `an activity for children under 12` `coaching, umpiring, refereeing or administration` `a program for equality of opportunity for a disadvantaged group` `equality of opportunity has been achieved` `I would require special services or facilities` `unreasonable to require them to supply them` `a Commissioner's exemption in force covers it` MEANS
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `s 21(5) -- no evidence produced that the animal is an assistance animal` THEN
        `within` `because I have the animal` `then if` `I did not produce evidence when asked`
    WHEN `s 50 -- a legal incapacity` THEN
        `within` `I am subject to a legal incapacity` `then if` `it is relevant to the transaction`
    WHEN `s 51 -- religious bodies` THEN
        `within` `religious ordination, training or observance` `then if` TRUE
    WHEN `s 52 -- a charitable provision in a will, deed or other instrument` THEN
        `within` `giving effect to a charitable provision` `then if` TRUE
    WHEN `s 53 -- complying with a law, order, award, agreement or the Commissioner` THEN
        `within` `necessary to comply with or authorised by a law, order, award, agreement or the Commissioner` `then if` TRUE
    WHEN `s 54 -- rights given for another person's pregnancy or childbirth` THEN
        `yes or no` `only because they gave rights to another person for pregnancy or childbirth`
    WHEN `s 55 -- public health` THEN
        `within` (a EQUALS `disability`) `then if` `reasonably necessary to protect public health`
    WHEN `s 56 -- competitive sport` THEN
        IF NOT `restricting who takes part in a competitive sporting activity`
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE IF `coaching, umpiring, refereeing or administration`
             THEN JUST FALSE
             ELSE CONSIDER `the restriction`
                  WHEN `to people of one sex` THEN
                      `yes or no` (`reasonable for the strength, stamina or physique required` AND (NOT `an activity for children under 12`))
                  WHEN `on another basis` THEN NOTHING
                  OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 57 -- a special measure` THEN
        `within` `a program for equality of opportunity for a disadvantaged group` `then if` (NOT `equality of opportunity has been achieved`)
    WHEN `s 58 -- accommodating a special need would be unreasonable` THEN
        `yes or no` (`I would require special services or facilities` AND `unreasonable to require them to supply them`)
    WHEN `s 59 -- an exemption granted by the Commissioner` THEN
        `within` `a Commissioner's exemption in force covers it` `then if` TRUE

§§ `ss 116, 122, 123, 126, 128 -- which version of the Act applies`

DECLARE `Which law applies` IS ONE OF
    `the Act does not apply: the conduct took place before 1 August 1993 (s 116)`
    `the Act as it stood before 3 July 2023 applies (ss 122, 123); not encoded here`
    `this encoding applies, but your complaint is dealt with under Part 6 as it stood when you made it (s 128); not encoded here`
    `this encoding applies, except that s 20A as it stood before 31 October 2025 applies, with a strict 12-month limit (s 126)`
    `s 20A as it stood before 31 October 2025 applies (s 126), and your complaint is dealt with under Part 6 as it stood when you made it (s 128); neither is encoded here`
    `this encoding applies`

-- s 116(1): the Act "does not apply to prohibited conduct which took place before the commencement". s 122: "This Act, as
-- in force before the commencement, continues to apply in relation to a complaint that was made before the commencement"
-- (3 July 2023); s 123(1): the 2022 amendments "do not apply to prohibited conduct ... that took place before the
-- commencement". s 126(1): for a complaint made after 31 October 2025 "about an act done before the commencement", s 20A
-- "as in force immediately before the commencement" continues to apply, with the 12-month limit and (2) without the
-- Commissioner's s 65(2) power. s 128: a pending individual complaint made before 27 July 2026 is determined under
-- Part 6 as in force before then (assumed pending and individual: fork F8).
GIVEN `the day of the conduct` IS A DATE
      `it is about inciting hatred (s 20A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a complaint has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the complaint` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Which law applies`
`transitional -- which law applies` `the day of the conduct` `it is about inciting hatred (s 20A)` `a complaint has been made` `the day of the complaint` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the day of the conduct` `is before` `the commencement day` THEN `the Act does not apply: the conduct took place before 1 August 1993 (s 116)`
        IF `the day of the conduct` `is before` `the 2022 amendments day` THEN `the Act as it stood before 3 July 2023 applies (ss 122, 123); not encoded here`
        IF `a complaint has been made` AND (`the day of the complaint` `is before` `the 2022 amendments day`) THEN `the Act as it stood before 3 July 2023 applies (ss 122, 123); not encoded here`
        IF `old s 20A` AND `old Part 6` THEN `s 20A as it stood before 31 October 2025 applies (s 126), and your complaint is dealt with under Part 6 as it stood when you made it (s 128); neither is encoded here`
        IF `old s 20A` THEN `this encoding applies, except that s 20A as it stood before 31 October 2025 applies, with a strict 12-month limit (s 126)`
        IF `old Part 6` THEN `this encoding applies, but your complaint is dealt with under Part 6 as it stood when you made it (s 128); not encoded here`
        OTHERWISE `this encoding applies`
    WHERE
        `old s 20A` MEANS `it is about inciting hatred (s 20A)` AND (`the day of the conduct` `is before` `the 2025 amendments day`)
        `old Part 6` MEANS `a complaint has been made` AND (`the day of the complaint` `is before` `the 2025 Part 3 day`)

§§ `s 60 and the bars on complaining again`

DECLARE `Who is complaining` IS ONE OF
    `the person aggrieved by the prohibited conduct`
    `a person authorised in writing by the Commissioner, on behalf of the person aggrieved`
    `an organisation or body, about systemic discrimination`
    `someone else`

DECLARE `Earlier complaint` IS ONE OF
    `no earlier complaint about the same conduct`
    `declined by the Commissioner after assessment (s 66)`
    `declined because no further action could be taken (s 66E)`
    `withdrawn (s 71)`
    `lapsed because I did not say I wished to continue (s 72)`
    `lapsed because I did not ask in time for referral to the Tribunal (s 81(6))`
    `declined as frivolous, trivial or misconceived, or as dealt with elsewhere (ss 67, 68)`

-- s 60: "Subject to this Act, the following may make a complaint to the Commissioner: (a) a person aggrieved by
-- prohibited conduct; (b) a person, authorised in writing by the Commissioner, on behalf of a person referred to in
-- paragraph (a); (c) an organisation or body ..., in relation to systemic discrimination." The bars: s 66D(1)(b) "the
-- complainant cannot make another complaint in relation to the same conduct", but (2) the Commissioner "may give
-- permission for a representative complaint declined under section 66 to be made again"; s 66F: not after a s 66E
-- decline "unless the Commissioner gives the complainant permission"; s 71(4): "Except with the permission of the
-- Commissioner, a complainant who withdraws a complaint ... shall not make another complaint"; s 72(3): after a lapse,
-- "the complainant shall not make another complaint in relation to the same conduct" (no permission); s 81(6): "the
-- complaint lapses and the complainant cannot make a further complaint" (no permission). Answers: NOTHING for someone
-- else (s 60's list grants, with no "only": NOTHING-kind: limited by its own wording) and after a s 67 or s 68 decline
-- (NOTHING-kind: silent, finding 6); JUST FALSE where a bar applies; JUST TRUE otherwise.
GIVEN who IS A `Who is complaining`
      `the earlier complaint` IS AN `Earlier complaint`
      `the Commissioner gave permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60 -- the complaint may be made` who `the earlier complaint` `the Commissioner gave permission` MEANS
    IF who EQUALS `someone else`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the earlier complaint`
         WHEN `no earlier complaint about the same conduct` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `declined by the Commissioner after assessment (s 66)` THEN
             `yes or no` ((who EQUALS `an organisation or body, about systemic discrimination`) AND `the Commissioner gave permission`)
         WHEN `declined because no further action could be taken (s 66E)` THEN `yes or no` `the Commissioner gave permission`
         WHEN `withdrawn (s 71)` THEN `yes or no` `the Commissioner gave permission`
         WHEN `lapsed because I did not say I wished to continue (s 72)` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `lapsed because I did not ask in time for referral to the Tribunal (s 81(6))` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `declined as frivolous, trivial or misconceived, or as dealt with elsewhere (ss 67, 68)` THEN NOTHING

§§ `Regulative rules for the complainant's steps`

-- The complainant's steps with a time limit are modelled as obligations: MUST take the step WITHIN the days allowed,
-- with the consequence the Act gives on failure. The helper runs a rule over the day of the step: on the stable l4 a
-- CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH, so FULFILLED means in time and anything else too late. It
-- takes a DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the complainant`
    `the Commissioner`

DECLARE `Step` IS ONE OF
    `make the complaint`
    `accept the complaint out of time`
    `request referral to the Tribunal`
    `extend the time for the request`
    `indicate a wish to continue`

GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
      `the actor` IS A `Party`
      `the step` IS A `Step`
      `the time of the step` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the step satisfies` `the rule` `by` `the actor` `doing` `the step` `at` `the time of the step` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time of the step`), (EVENT `the actor` `the step` `the time of the step`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `s 65 -- the time limit for making a complaint`

-- s 65(1): "a complaint must be made not later than 12 months after the alleged prohibited conduct took place." (1A): "a
-- representative complaint must be made not later than 24 months after an instance of the systemic discrimination
-- alleged in the complaint occurred." (2): "The Commissioner may accept a complaint after the time ... has expired if the
-- Commissioner is satisfied it is appropriate to do so." s 126: for a complaint about an act before 31 October 2025
-- under s 20A, the 12 months apply and "(2) The Commissioner's power in section 65(2) does not apply". "Not later than 12
-- months after" day D is read as ending on the anniversary of D (fork F1).
GIVEN `a representative complaint` IS A BOOLEAN
      `about a s 20A act before 31 October 2025` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the conduct` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 65 -- the last day to complain` `a representative complaint` `about a s 20A act before 31 October 2025` `the day of the conduct` MEANS
    IF `a representative complaint` AND (NOT `about a s 20A act before 31 October 2025`)
    THEN `the anniversary` 2 `years after` `the day of the conduct`
    ELSE `the anniversary` 1 `years after` `the day of the conduct`

-- The time limit with the s 65(2) power: MUST make the complaint WITHIN the days allowed, LEST the Commissioner MAY accept
-- it out of time.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`the complaint must be made within` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the complainant`
    MUST `make the complaint`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST
        PARTY `the Commissioner`
        MAY `accept the complaint out of time`

-- The time limit under s 126(2), with no power to accept a late complaint.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`the complaint must be made strictly within` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the complainant`
    MUST `make the complaint`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the complainant` BECAUSE "the 12 months for a complaint about an act before 31 October 2025 under s 20A have passed, and the Commissioner cannot accept it late (s 126(2))"

DECLARE `Complaint timing` IS ONE OF
    `in time`
    `late, but the Commissioner may still accept it if satisfied that is appropriate (s 65(2))`
    `late, and the Commissioner cannot accept it (s 126(2))`
    `not answered: that day is before the conduct`

GIVEN `a representative complaint` IS A BOOLEAN
      `about a s 20A act before 31 October 2025` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the conduct` IS A DATE
      `the day of complaining` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Complaint timing`
`s 65 -- the complaint is in time` `a representative complaint` `about a s 20A act before 31 October 2025` `the day of the conduct` `the day of complaining` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the day of complaining` `is before` `the day of the conduct` THEN `not answered: that day is before the conduct`
        IF `about a s 20A act before 31 October 2025` THEN
            IF `the step satisfies` (`the complaint must be made strictly within` `the days allowed here`) `by` `the complainant` `doing` `make the complaint` `at` `the time of complaining`
            THEN `in time`
            ELSE `late, and the Commissioner cannot accept it (s 126(2))`
        OTHERWISE
            IF `the step satisfies` (`the complaint must be made within` `the days allowed here`) `by` `the complainant` `doing` `make the complaint` `at` `the time of complaining`
            THEN `in time`
            ELSE `late, but the Commissioner may still accept it if satisfied that is appropriate (s 65(2))`
    WHERE
        `the days allowed here` MEANS `the days from` `the day of the conduct` `to` (`s 65 -- the last day to complain` `a representative complaint` `about a s 20A act before 31 October 2025` `the day of the conduct`)
        `the time of complaining` MEANS `the days from` `the day of the conduct` `to` `the day of complaining`

§§ `s 66 -- the Commissioner's decision to accept or decline`

-- s 66(1): the Commissioner "must, after assessing a complaint, decide to accept or decline the complaint: (a) for a
-- representative complaint - no later than 90 days after receiving it; or (b) otherwise - no later than 60 days after
-- receiving it." (2): the complainant must be notified "as soon as practicable after making it". The day of receipt is
-- excluded, so the last day is the receipt day plus 60 (or 90) days.
GIVEN `a representative complaint` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 66 -- the last day for the decision` `a representative complaint` `the day received` MEANS
    IF `a representative complaint`
    THEN `the date` 90 `days after` `the day received`
    ELSE `the date` 60 `days after` `the day received`

§§ `s 72 -- a complaint the complainant seems to have lost interest in`

-- s 72(1): if the Commissioner is satisfied the complainant has lost interest, the Commissioner "shall advise the
-- complainant in writing that the complaint will lapse unless the complainant indicates that the complainant wishes to
-- continue with it." (2): "If a complainant ... does not give an indication within 60 days that the complainant wishes to
-- continue with the complaint, the complaint lapses". (3): no further complaint about the same conduct. Counted from the
-- day of being advised, that day excluded (fork F1).
GIVEN `the day I was advised` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 72 -- the last day to say I wish to continue` `the day I was advised` MEANS `the date` 60 `days after` `the day I was advised`

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`the wish to continue must be indicated within` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the complainant`
    MUST `indicate a wish to continue`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the complainant` BECAUSE "no indication within 60 days: the complaint lapses and no further complaint may be made about the same conduct (s 72(2), (3))"

DECLARE `Continuing outcome` IS ONE OF
    `the complaint continues`
    `the complaint lapses, and you cannot complain again about the same conduct (s 72(2), (3))`
    `not answered: that day is before you were advised`

GIVEN `the day I was advised` IS A DATE, `the day I say so` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Continuing outcome`
`s 72 -- the outcome` `the day I was advised` `the day I say so` MEANS
    IF `the day I say so` `is before` `the day I was advised`
    THEN `not answered: that day is before you were advised`
    ELSE IF `the step satisfies` (`the wish to continue must be indicated within` (`the days from` `the day I was advised` `to` (`s 72 -- the last day to say I wish to continue` `the day I was advised`))) `by` `the complainant` `doing` `indicate a wish to continue` `at` (`the days from` `the day I was advised` `to` `the day I say so`)
         THEN `the complaint continues`
         ELSE `the complaint lapses, and you cannot complain again about the same conduct (s 72(2), (3))`

§§ `ss 79, 80 -- a direction to attend conciliation`

DECLARE `Conciliation consequence` IS ONE OF
    `nothing follows: there was no written direction, or you complied with it`
    `nothing follows: you had a reasonable excuse (ss 79(6), 80(1))`
    `the Commissioner may dismiss your complaint and direct you to pay the respondent's costs (s 80(1)(a)), and not complying is an offence with a maximum penalty of 100 penalty units (s 79(4))`

-- s 79(1), (2): the Commissioner "may direct a person to take part in a conciliation"; the direction "must be in writing
-- and specify the time when and place where the conciliation will be held." (4): not complying is an offence, "Maximum
-- penalty: 100 penalty units", of strict liability (5), with a defence of reasonable excuse (6). s 80(1): "If, without
-- reasonable excuse, a party ... does not comply ..., the Commissioner may, where the party is: (a) the complainant,
-- dismiss the complaint and may direct the complainant to pay to the respondent such costs as the Commissioner thinks
-- fit". (2): the costs may be registered as a judgment debt. A direction that is not in writing with a time and place is
-- read as not a direction under s 79 (fork F6).
GIVEN `a written direction with a time and place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I complied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Conciliation consequence`
`ss 79, 80 -- what follows` `a written direction with a time and place` `I complied` `I had a reasonable excuse` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `a written direction with a time and place`) OR `I complied` THEN `nothing follows: there was no written direction, or you complied with it`
        IF `I had a reasonable excuse` THEN `nothing follows: you had a reasonable excuse (ss 79(6), 80(1))`
        OTHERWISE `the Commissioner may dismiss your complaint and direct you to pay the respondent's costs (s 80(1)(a)), and not complying is an offence with a maximum penalty of 100 penalty units (s 79(4))`

-- s 79(4): the maximum penalty, in penalty units (the value of a unit is set under the Penalty Units Act, not deposited).
`s 79 -- the maximum penalty in penalty units` MEANS 100

§§ `s 81 -- asking for referral to the Tribunal`

-- s 81(3): "If an individual complaint is not resolved by conciliation, the complainant may request the Commissioner to
-- refer the complaint to the Tribunal for hearing." (4): "The request must be made within 21 days after receiving the
-- Commissioner's notification under subsections (2) and (2A)." (5): the time may be extended. (6): if the request is not
-- made in time, "the complaint lapses and the complainant cannot make a further complaint in relation to the same
-- conduct." s 86: Division 4A "does not apply to a representative complaint". s 87(1): the Commissioner "must refer a
-- complaint that has been accepted under section 66 ... if the complainant requests". The last day is the day of
-- receipt plus 21 days (fork F1), or the extended day.
DECLARE `Referral deadline` IS ONE OF
    `the last day to ask is` HAS `the last referral day` IS A DATE
    `a representative complaint is not referred to the Tribunal (s 86)`

GIVEN `a representative complaint` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I received the notification` IS A DATE
      `the time was extended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the extended last day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Referral deadline`
`s 81 -- the referral deadline` `a representative complaint` `the day I received the notification` `the time was extended` `the extended last day` MEANS
    IF `a representative complaint`
    THEN `a representative complaint is not referred to the Tribunal (s 86)`
    ELSE IF `the time was extended`
         THEN `the last day to ask is` `the extended last day`
         ELSE `the last day to ask is` (`the date` 21 `days after` `the day I received the notification`)

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`the referral must be requested within` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the complainant`
    MUST `request referral to the Tribunal`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the complainant` BECAUSE "no request within the time allowed: the complaint lapses and no further complaint may be made about the same conduct (s 81(6))"

DECLARE `Referral outcome` IS ONE OF
    `in time: the Commissioner must refer your complaint to the Tribunal (s 87(1))`
    `too late: the complaint lapses, and you cannot complain again about the same conduct (s 81(6))`
    `a representative complaint cannot be referred to the Tribunal (s 86)`
    `not answered: that day is before you received the notification`

GIVEN `a representative complaint` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I received the notification` IS A DATE
      `the time was extended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the extended last day` IS A DATE
      `the day I ask` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Referral outcome`
`s 81 -- the referral outcome` `a representative complaint` `the day I received the notification` `the time was extended` `the extended last day` `the day I ask` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 81 -- the referral deadline` `a representative complaint` `the day I received the notification` `the time was extended` `the extended last day`
    WHEN `a representative complaint is not referred to the Tribunal (s 86)` THEN `a representative complaint cannot be referred to the Tribunal (s 86)`
    WHEN `the last day to ask is` `the final day` THEN
        IF `the day I ask` `is before` `the day I received the notification`
        THEN `not answered: that day is before you received the notification`
        ELSE IF `the step satisfies` (`the referral must be requested within` (`the days from` `the day I received the notification` `to` `the final day`)) `by` `the complainant` `doing` `request referral to the Tribunal` `at` (`the days from` `the day I received the notification` `to` `the day I ask`)
             THEN `in time: the Commissioner must refer your complaint to the Tribunal (s 87(1))`
             ELSE `too late: the complaint lapses, and you cannot complain again about the same conduct (s 81(6))`

§§ `s 88 -- compensation the Tribunal may order`

-- s 88(1)(b): "an order requiring the respondent to pay to the complainant or another person, within a specified period,
-- an amount, being an amount not more than that prescribed, that the Tribunal considers appropriate as compensation for
-- loss or damage caused by the prohibited conduct". (3): "damage ... includes the offence, embarrassment, humiliation,
-- and intimidation suffered by the person." (4): if the conduct "is not substantiated the Tribunal shall make an order
-- dismissing the complaint." The prescribed maximum is set by regulation under s 117, which is not deposited: it is an
-- input. Answers: JUST FALSE where not substantiated ("shall make an order dismissing") or above the maximum ("not more
-- than"); JUST TRUE otherwise (what the Tribunal "considers appropriate" is its judgment).
GIVEN `the Tribunal found it substantiated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the prescribed maximum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 88 -- the Tribunal may order this compensation` `the Tribunal found it substantiated` `the amount` `the prescribed maximum` MEANS
    `yes or no` (`the Tribunal found it substantiated` AND `the amount` AT MOST `the prescribed maximum`)

§§ `s 106 -- appeal to the Supreme Court`

-- s 106(1): "a party aggrieved by the decision or order of the Tribunal" may appeal. (2): "An appeal may be on a question
-- of law or fact or law and fact and must be made: (a) within 28 days after the day on which the decision or order was
-- made; or (b) if the Tribunal did not give written reasons at the time the decision or order was made, and the party
-- making the appeal subsequently requests the Tribunal to do so, not later than 28 days after the day on which the party
-- received the reasons in writing." The day is excluded, so the last day is that day plus 28; where (b) applies its later
-- day is the limit (fork F7).
GIVEN `the day of the decision` IS A DATE
      `written reasons given at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I asked for written reasons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I received them` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 106 -- the last day to appeal` `the day of the decision` `written reasons given at the time` `I asked for written reasons` `the day I received them` MEANS
    IF (NOT `written reasons given at the time`) AND `I asked for written reasons`
    THEN `the date` 28 `days after` `the day I received them`
    ELSE `the date` 28 `days after` `the day of the decision`
